<item><title>Lahaiba FA beat Medina FC 4-3 on penalties to win SESDO League Cup</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/lahaiba-fa-beat-medina-fc-4-3-on-penalties-to-win-sesdo-fb7b24/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/lahaiba-fa-beat-medina-fc-4-3-on-penalties-to-win-sesdo-fb7b24/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>Lahaiba FA won the Serrekunda East Sports Development Organization (SESDO) 2026 Africell League Cup after a goalless draw, taking the penalty shootout 4-3 at the East Mini Stadium.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:17:34 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Gambia election: Nine cleared for December 5 vote</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambia-election-nine-cleared-for-december-5-vote-f6d7c1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambia-election-nine-cleared-for-december-5-vote-f6d7c1/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>Incumbent Adama Barrow and veteran opposition leader Ousainou Darboe are among the nine candidates cleared to stand.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:51:25 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambia-election-nine-cleared-for-december-5-vote-f6d7c1/share.jpg" length="37534" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambia-election-nine-cleared-for-december-5-vote-f6d7c1/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Gambia&apos;s NDP accuses electoral commission of opacity over Bojang candidacy</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambia-s-ndp-accuses-electoral-commission-of-opacity-over-82a2a9/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambia-s-ndp-accuses-electoral-commission-of-opacity-over-82a2a9/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>The National Democratic Party says the Independent Electoral Commission denied its representatives access to its premises while they sought details of leader Kebba Madi Bojang&apos;s.</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:16:13 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Gambian parties and stakeholders sign Janjanbureh peace accord before December vote</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambian-parties-and-stakeholders-sign-janjanbureh-peace-9e33fb/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambian-parties-and-stakeholders-sign-janjanbureh-peace-9e33fb/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>The revised accord commits parties to peaceful, inclusive and credible polls on December 5, with the EU planning an independent observer mission.</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:01:40 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
